Z||000000||fierofrek||06-08-2001||01:05 PM||||ok, I know what parts I will need for doing a inline 4 to a V6 conversion, what I don't know is this.<P>*) a buddy from a local car club says that you have to keep the brain (ecm) for the inline 4 in the car, and "mate" the V6 brain to the wiring harness to work the motor.<P>correct me if I'm wrong, but wont this cause some problems between the ECMs? like the inline 4 brain trying to control a motor that is not connected, and a V6 brain trying to control gauges and stuff that are not connected?<P>I thank you for any help you can give as I don't want a screwed up car. hehehe.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fierofrek (edited 06-08-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||06-08-2001||02:28 PM||||If it's a normal Fiero V-6, just remove the entire 4 cyl ECM and engine harness, and install the V-6 ECM. I've heard rumors of some other conversions using both ECMs, but I'm not sure how that would work out.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierofrek||06-08-2001||03:20 PM||||kewl, thx for the help! you just saved me alot of headaches! hehe||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||06-08-2001||08:53 PM||||Ooops. If your car is an 84, I understand it's a lot more of a PITA. Lots of wiring changes after 84. Hope I didn't mess you up.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
